From 4d344cf99f93deb50c051e71ddeb7dd176d5d799 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vincent Leon <leon@mbp.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:29:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] feat(android): keep the daemon connection alive in the
 background

On HarmonyOS's Android compatibility layer, and under aggressive vendor
battery management, a backgrounded Paseo is frozen and loses its daemon
connection. Without Google services it gets no push either, so nothing
arrives until it is opened again.

Add a Stay connected in background switch (General settings, Android
only) backed by a local Expo module. It holds a specialUse foreground
service with a quiet ongoing notification, which keeps the process, the
connection and the local attention notifications it raises alive.
specialUse rather than dataSync, which Android 15 stops after six hours.
Turning it on also asks for the battery optimization exemption, since
Doze and vendor battery managers can still cut an optimized app's
network with the screen off. Swiping Paseo out of recents ends the
service. Off by default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
